      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-23T10:29:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have an extra step of `pkvm_host_donate_hyp_share_ro` here. We could wrap it in the alloc function, but `topup_pkvm_memcache` returns only -ENOMEM regardless of what the error is. Is it okay to keep it as it is?",
      "parentUuid": "8f4917cf_d26f0aeb",
      "revId": "d6787ef07c3fc52b17aa0035ffd50f16e1566e1e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62ad3afb_598434d7",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/domain.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 144,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-23T12:09:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do the same in pvMMU (with the only difference that we use regular pkvm_host_donate_hyp()), and pKVM-ARM does the same, in both MMU and IOMMU code. So it seems better to do the same, for consistency and to avoid error-prone duplication of logic? Failing pkvm_host_donate_hyp_share_ro() shouldn\u0027t normally happen anyway, and we at least have a WARN_ON for it.\n\nBTW if we keep it as is, it is not much better in term of the returned error either, since for some reason you are returning -EBUSY regardless of the actual error returned? :)",
      "parentUuid": "1f1f0257_1f1b90bd",
      "revId": "d6787ef07c3fc52b17aa0035ffd50f16e1566e1e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
